vendor/pi-jev-model-router contains the byte-identical selected upstream
archive (package.json, LICENSE, README.md, extensions, test, tsconfig.json),
plus an UPSTREAM_COMMIT provenance marker. The upstream MIT license is
preserved both there and in the root LICENSE.

src/core contains adapted production modules derived from upstream config,
jev, router, budget, and ranking. Changes include exact-provider matching,
exact budget accumulation and client/privacy hardening, documented in
README.md and docs/policy-adaptations.md and related contracts. These current
production modules are not claimed to be byte-identical to upstream.
test/core contains adapted tests with local import paths and isolated resource
setup. Only the selected immutable vendor archive is baseline byte-identical.
The vendored parent extension is reference material only; it is not registered
or loaded as this package's extension. Attribution does not establish full
routing parity or acceptance.

The preexisting upstream-patches directory retains its own Pi and Tintin
license and provenance notices; those patches are separate prerequisites.
